}

/* -- idle reply placeholder: shrink so it fits one line (problem 2) ------ *
 * The idle "可先草拟回复,或点 ✎ 插话…" placeholder rides the 16px form-field
 * floor (the iOS-zoom guard above), which on a phone wraps to two lines in the
 * default single-line (collapsed) textarea. Shrink ONLY the placeholder so the
 * hint fits one line; the textarea's own 16px input text is left untouched, so
 * real typing keeps the iOS-zoom guard and the normal input size. Paired with
 * the shortened placeholder string (app.js). Desktop is unaffected. */
#flow-reply-input::placeholder {
  font-size: 13px;
}

/* -- docked reply meta: tile head + prompt toggle on one row (G2) ------- *
 * Desktop stacks the reply-context children vertically (the TO/KIND head
 * row, then the "▸ 展开消息详情" prompt toggle row, then the options row),
 * wasting the right-side whitespace and eating vertical room. On a phone lay
 * the active context out as a wrapping row so the head and the prompt toggle
 * share one line; the expandable prompt body and the options buttons drop to
 * their own full-width rows below. The expanded `.flow-reply-prompt` keeps its
 * `max-height: 30vh` internal scroll (defined at the top level). */
#flow-view .flow-reply-context.active {
  flex-direction: row;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: baseline;
  column-gap: 10px;
}
#flow-view .flow-reply-context.active .flow-reply-head {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
}
#flow-view .flow-reply-context.active .flow-reply-prompt-wrap {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;

